On Feb 21, 6:54 am, "slayer88" <slayergwarironmai...@yahoo.com> wrote:
> I'm new to nethack and I am addicted to it. Does anyone know what the
> all around best class is?

The best class for winning is Valkyrie. But to be able to win you need
a lot of knowledge skill and patience. It is normally useful to read
spoilers, but you may want to discover things on your own. If you want
to discover on your own just remember that Nethack has too many things
and you will discover new things even if you have read all the
spoilers.

In general in the beginning you would like to pick up skills that will
help you get proficient at the game and then play to win.

I would recommend two practice games which will give you different
skills.

The most important beginning skill is to use your pet, have patience
and learn to run away.  Its not doom, and its not necessary to kill
other monsters.

You should play a gnomish healer without trying to hit any monster,
reach the minetown without gaining any experience levels. Using just
Elbereth and your pet.

After that you will want to play an Orcish Ranger. This guy does not
have any direct attacks. You will learn and appreciate attacking from
a distance picking up your fights.  In this game you should not try to
kill all monster but use your pets, but you can and should kill any
monsters that are dangerous for your pets. In this game you should go
to the Sokoban first and then return to Minetown. You should do this
within XL 7.

In this game you will learn how to pickup your own fights, you will
appreciate attacking with ranged weapons. You will also find that they
disappear and you will learn to use them carefully. Using pets in
Sokoban is helpful in gaining more pet use proficiency, and
carefulness.

Next you should try to play a wizard as a wizard is also a different
type of game. Get a little bit used to it, and then attempt a win with
a Valkyrie. All the skills that you pick in the other games will come
of use there.

